# tests/test_weather.py compares to_bytes() output against this fixture
# byte-for-byte, and to_bytes() deliberately produces CRLF line endings (the
# on-disk encoding real .WPR writers use). Without this, core.autocrlf
# silently rewrites those CRLFs to LF on `git add` (measured: a committed
# blob loses every CR) and, on a checkout where autocrlf does not mirror the
# committing machine's setting, they never come back -- breaking the
# byte-exact comparison. -text disables that conversion unconditionally.
tests/fixtures/weather/*.WPR -text
